  "functions": [
    "FUNC.LARGE"
  ],
  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "LARGE validates unrounded k against [1, n] before truncating (n + 1 - k) and preserves qualified overflow numbers",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527, LARGE(array, k) validates the unrounded numeric k against 1 <= k <= n (returning #NUM! when k > n even if trunc(k) == n, such as k = 1 + 2^-52 on a 1-element array) before indexing ascending sorted values at trunc(n + 1.0 - k) (whose stored subtraction rounds ranks adjacent to an integer), skips text, logicals, and blanks inside arrays or ranges, and preserves qualified overflow numbers. Matches 2,848/2,848 full-bank LARGE rows.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in Excel 16.0.20527.20088 in prefix_metadata (row 139) and across 2,848/2,848 full-bank LARGE rows in CalcFunc-Evidence (bank2-answers-large-{more,scalar,special}.json).",
